      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Lorenzo. With this approach, the ipServer created will have the Type#TETHERING_LOCAL_HOTSPOT  based on WifiIpMode received as part of WiFiManager broadcast event.\n\nThe TetheringInterface formed as part of these events (onLocalOnlyInterfacesChanged / onTetheredInterfacesChanged) will have the type picked from IpServer and TYPE_LOCAL_HOTSPOT will be send @ https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/Tethering.java;l\u003d1099?q\u003dTethering.java\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject \n\nFor the TetheringEventCallback#onClientsChanged events, only TYPE_WIFI is considered and if the additional LOCAL_HOTSPOT conditional check will fix this as well @ https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Connectivity/Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/ConnectedClientsTracker.java;l\u003d92-111?q\u003dupdateConnectedClients\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject\n\nRegarding the scope, as of the default scope is GLOBAL except for TYPE_NCM and making the scope local for TYPE_LOCAL_HOTSPOT and allowing TYPE_LOCAL_HOTSPOT in checkConnectivityScope will handle the scenarios.\n\nI will upload a patch in a day for review.",
